<spell-notebook "statistic theming">
	<header level="1">
		Statistic
		<header>A statistic emphasizes the current value of an attribute.</>
	</>
	<statistic-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-statistic-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a `<ui-statistics>`
			group, `:root`), or on the box through `::part(statistic)` (the group's box is `::part(group)`). They inherit into
			the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- `--ui-statistic-value-size` and `--ui-statistic-text-value-size` replace the size ladder's value sizes;
			  `direction="horizontal"` swaps in its own ladder.
			- The `value` and `label` parts style the shorthands.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-statistics {
			  --ui-statistic-horizontal-spacing: 2.5em;
			  --ui-statistic-row-spacing: 2em;
			}
			ui-statistic::part(label) {
			  text-transform: none;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`color` remaps `--ui-color` for the value; `size` picks a step of the value-size ladder. Never set the
				`--_ui-*` / `--_statistic-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-statistic" playground>
				<ui-statistic value="5,550" label="Downloads"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
